      "message": "Not necessarily, during the initial boot, RK3399\u0027s GPIO wasn\u0027t configured, the trackpad, Lid sensor, DMIC, and ALC5514 have not been configured by the system . That\u0027s when the leakage might happens. Whereas in susped /resume, before we suspend, we can configure GPIO and configure component properly to reduce leakage. \n\nAgain, this is just a risk, I will work with Samsung termi to quickly check out. If no major issue, then we are good to go with a nice state based sequencing.",
